The errors DELIVER to the awaits of the cancel/yield token onCancel futures! So when the token is cancelled, `onCancel`'s completion delivers... the ArgumentError as the error being propagated INTO the await?! No wait — the "registration stack" is where the LISTENER was registered; `handleError` runs the registered error callback... 

The KEY question remains: what future completes with an ERROR whose catchError handler mis-returns? The onCancel future is `Completer<void>.sync().future` — Future<void>. Its await registers value+error continuations. When completed with a VALUE, no error handler runs.

UNLESS the future completed with an ERROR — does anything complete onCancel with an error? `completer.complete()` only.

